cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the archived release and the manuscript below."
type: software
title: "Reproduction package: unsupervised and semi-supervised anomaly detection for credit card fraud under chronological evaluation"
abstract: >
  Revision pipeline (v2) for the manuscript "Unsupervised and Semi-Supervised
  Anomaly Detection for Credit Card Fraud: A Chronological Benchmark and a
  Hybrid Bridge to Supervised Learning". Benchmarks five classical detectors
  (Isolation Forest, LOF, One-Class SVM, DBSCAN, K-Means) on two public fraud
  datasets (ULB creditcard.csv and PaySim) under a leakage-free chronological
  protocol: explicit out-of-sample scoring for LOF and DBSCAN, decision
  thresholds fitted on validation and applied unchanged to the test stream, and
  three named fitting regimes (label-free, normal-only, oracle). The scripts of
  the submitted version are included unmodified for auditability.
